Subject: [PATCH] Exynos8895: preserve SCSI sense on misleading UFS OCS

The SM-G955N records OCS 7 for commands with a valid CHECK CONDITION
response, including an unsupported MODE SENSE subpage. Use the same
UFS core workaround as the other affected Exynos hosts so that the
SCSI midlayer sees the device sense and applies its normal fallback.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -2319,6 +2319,7 @@
 	.uic_attr = &exynos8895_uic_attr,
 	.quirks = UFSHCD_QUIRK_PRDT_BYTE_GRAN |
 		  UFSHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_REQ_LIST_CLR |
+		  UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_OCS_FATAL_ERROR |
 		  UFSHCI_QUIRK_SKIP_RESET_INTR_AGGR,
 	.opts = EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_BROKEN_AUTO_CLK_CTRL |
 		EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_SKIP_CONFIG_PHY_ATTR |
